What RG DS Play's checkpoints need from Caprice32.

- A state keeps the tape's place: a trailer after the snapshot (cap32/tape.c
  rgds_tape_state_save/_load), so a multiload tape game resumed between its loads,
  or during one, goes on where it was. States without one still load.
- A state load restores PPI port C: the snapshot loader wrote the PPI control word
  after the ports, and setting a mode clears an 8255's ports, so every load lost
  port C (the tape motor, the PSG's control lines, the keyboard row). Control
  first now.
- retro_rgds_loading() is true while the autorun is still typing the game's
  command, which no state holds; RG DS Play saves no checkpoint then.
- retro_rgds_cancel_autorun() drops a queued autorun command: a state loaded right
  after the game starts would otherwise have RUN"... typed into the resumed game.

